   "source": [
    "## Chapter 1 — Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "Renewable energy capacity in India varies by state and by technology, including bio-mass, small hydro, solar, wind and waste-to-energy. A state-level model can help describe historical patterns and estimate the next year's total installed capacity.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Questions addressed\n",
    "1. How does total installed renewable capacity change across years?\n",
    "2. Which renewable technologies contribute the largest capacity totals in this dataset?\n",
    "3. Which states/regions have the largest recorded total in the latest year?\n",
    "4. Can previous-year capacity, population and GSDP help estimate next-year total capacity?\n",
    "\n",
    "### Modelling decision\n",
    "The uploaded file has five installed-capacity columns. These are combined into one target. The current year's five component columns are **not** used as predictors because doing so would reveal the answer. Instead, their previous-year values are used as lag features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a99f16c5",
   "metadata": {},
